title: Instructions/list_wikis

''Route mode only.'' Lists the wiki servers the router can reach right now, one per line:

```
- bundler (label mcp-bundler) http://localhost:8080, pid 15356
- uni-link (label mcp-uni-link) http://localhost:8081, pid 20412
```

* The first word is the folder name. Pass it, the label or the port as the `wiki` argument of any other tool
* A server started without `listen` or `sse` shows `no HTTP`
* Servers come and go. The list is read fresh on every call, from the `.tw-mcp/connect` files below the `route=` folder

Takes no parameters. See [[Several Wikis From One Client (Route Mode)|Instructions]].

''Example prompts:''

* "Which wikis are running?"
* "Run this filter in the uni-link wiki."
